---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import glyph from '../brand/glyph.svg?raw';
const goals = [
  'Run it yourself, in your own Cloudflare account.',
  'Nothing else to host or look after.',
  'Fill in the week, submit it, get it approved.',
  'Your hours export as CSV, any time.',
  'Open source, under the AGPL-3.0 licence.',
];
const features = [
  'A weekly grid with a note on each cell, and keyboard entry.',
  'Submit, return with a reason, approve and lock, with a list of who has not submitted.',
  'Reports and a chart of hours by person, client, project, task and week.',
  'CSV export, and an import that previews before it writes.',
  'Add, offboard and reinstate people. Only admins and stewards create clients and projects.',
  'Passkeys, optional single sign-on, recovery codes and an admin re-enrolment link.',
  'Nightly encrypted backups to a second account, with a status view and a test alert.',
  'Agents can fill in a person\'s own week over MCP. Off unless you turn it on.',
  'Limits such as session length and import size, set as deploy variables.',
];
---
<Layout title="tidwick: weekly timesheets you run yourself" description="Weekly timesheets you run yourself, in your own Cloudflare account.">
  <div class="top">
  <section class="hero">
    <Fragment set:html={glyph} />
    <p class="kicker">weekly timesheets you run yourself</p>
    <h1>tidwick</h1>
    <p class="deck">A weekly timesheet for a professional-services firm. Someone technical deploys it to the firm's own Cloudflare account. Nobody hosts it for you.</p>
    <div class="ctas">
      <a class="cta primary" href="https://demo.tidwick.dev/demo">Try the demo</a>
      <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick">Run your own</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="goals">
    <h2 id="goals">Design goals</h2>
    <ol class="goals">
      {goals.map((g, i) => <li><span class="num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span>{g}</span></li>)}
    </ol>
  </section>
  </div>
  <section aria-labelledby="features" class="features">
    <h2 id="features">What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      {features.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
  <div class="tiles">
    <section class="tile">
      <h2>Try the demo</h2>
      <p>A running copy to look around in. Pick one of four invented people, with no sign-up. It resets every night.</p>
      <p>tidwick is version 0, tested only by its author, with no support commitment. It is not a hosted service, and it has no timer, calendar view, invoicing, rates or native apps.</p>
      <p><a href="https://demo.tidwick.dev/demo">Open demo.tidwick.dev</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="tile">
      <h2>Run your own</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#9-deploy">docs walk through</a> deploying tidwick to your own Cloudflare account. They assume the Workers Paid plan (the free plan is untested). You also need a domain, a second account for the off-account backup, and about an hour.</p>
      <p class="deploy">
        <a class="deploy-btn" href="https://deploy.workers.cloudflare.com/?url=https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick"><img src="/deploy-to-cloudflare.svg" alt="Deploy to Cloudflare" width="184" height="39" /></a>
      </p>
      <p>The button creates the Worker. It is untested on a real account. Then open the Worker's address: the setup page generates the keys in your browser, and a one-time setup token claims the first admin.</p>
      <p><strong>Why only Cloudflare?</strong> It runs entirely on Workers, D1, R2 and cron, so there is nothing else to host. <a href="https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick/blob/main/docs/adr/0001-cloudflare-astro-platform.md">ADR 0001</a> has the reasoning.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
